Modifications made on top of upstream (branch `feat/intranet`) include:

- Intranet network policy (`frontier_agent/infra/network_policy.py`):
  fail-closed by default (`FRONTIER_AGENT_INTRANET_ONLY=1`); outbound
  destinations must resolve to private networks; operator extension via
  `FRONTIER_AGENT_ALLOWED_NETWORK_HOSTS` / `FRONTIER_AGENT_ALLOWED_NETWORK_CIDRS`.
- Search channels for intranet use: DeepSeek-native and generic
  Anthropic-compatible search fallbacks in `plugins/tools/web_search.py`;
  aligned search/fetch implementations default to empty endpoints instead of
  public Serper/Jina.
- Data-exfiltration paths closed in intranet mode: `web_fetch`,
  `download_file`, E2B sandbox, remote OCR/Vision (opt-in), and model-authored
  shell network (sandbox `allow_net=False` / isolated-backend requirement).
- Writing-style rules for prose deliverables (distilled from the
  human-writing, tech-doc-style-chinese and weng-post writing skills) injected
  into the agent_team and stateful_react_agent workflow prompts and the TUI
  coding/research prompts, sourced from `workflows/_shared/writing_style.py`.
- Documentation additions: `docs/install/intranet-deployment.zh-CN.md`.

Upstream branding, documentation, and third-party notices in the source tree
are retained unchanged for provenance.